          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            the
            %em quantum master Ward identity
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnRegularPolynomialObservablesMasterWardIdentity"}
            below) expresses the relation between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum
            (measured by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℏ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+theory"} interacting
            (measured by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar, g\to 0
            (remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuantumMasterEuqationRelatesQuantumInteractingELEquationsToClassicalFreeELEquations"}
            below). As such it generalizes the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger-Dyson+equation"} Schwinger-Dyson equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 0
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuantumMasterEuqationRelatesQuantumInteractingELEquationsToClassicalFreeELEquations"}
            below) as well as the
            = succeed "," do
              %em classical master Ward identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar = 0
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MasterWardIdentityClassical"}
            below).
          %p
            Applied to products of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            with any given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
            = succeed "." do
              %em Ward identity
          %p
            This is of interest notably in view of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether%27s+theorem"} Noether's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetry+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetry of the Lagrangian
            of, in particular, the given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conserved current
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+differential+form"} horizontal differential form
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+spacetime+derivative"} total spacetime derivative
            vanishes up to a term proportional to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
            this is a relation of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi div
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %mtext on-shell
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  div \mathbf{J} = 0 \phantom{AAA} \text{on-shell}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where “on shell” means up to the ideal generated by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
            of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi div
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} div \mathbf{J}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conserved current
            to actually be conserved, due to both quantum effects (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            ) and interactions (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            ). This is the form in which Ward identities are usually understood (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NoetherCurrentConservationQuantumCorrection"}
            below).
          %p
            In terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+master+equation"} quantum master equation
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+polynomial+observables"} regular polynomial observables
            (
            %a{:href => "quantum+master+equation#QuantumMasterEquation"}> this prop.
            ).
          %p
            Neither of these equations is guaranteed to hold for any choice of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative QFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
            that preserves it, the one speaks of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conserved current
            corresponding to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetry"} gauge symmetry
            is
            %em anomalous
            in this way, one speaks of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+anomaly"} gauge anomaly
          %h2#details Details
          %h3#BeforeRenormalization Before renormalization
          #OnRegularPolynomialObservablesMasterWardIdentity.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_{\text{BV-BRST}}, \mathbf{L}')
              (
              %a{:href => "A+first+idea+of+quantum+field+theory#GaugeFixingLagrangianDensity"}> this def.
              ) with global
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-differential"} BV-differential
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+polynomial+observables"} regular polynomial observables
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi reg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PolyObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi reg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
