                    \\mathcal{R}^{-1}
                    \\left(
                    \\left\{ -(S' + g S_{int}) \,,\, A \right\}_{\mathcal{T}}
                    \-
                    i \hbar   \Delta_{BV}(A)
                    \\right)
                    \\;=\;
                    0
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\text{on-shell}
            %p
              In contrast, the left hand side is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+observable"} interacting field observable
              (via
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#MollerOperatorOnRegularPolynomialObservables"} this def.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+product"} time-ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antibracket"} antibracket
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+theory"} interacting field theory
              and a quantum correction given by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-operator"} BV-operator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-operator"} BV-operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi BV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{BV}
              (
              %a{:href => "BV-operator#RearrangedMasterWardWithOnShell"}> this def.
              ) we may equivalently re-write this as
            #eq:RearrangedMasterWardWithOnShell.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
